Overlay 0042: kill the multi-second boot black screen caused by
2S2H's DynamicCosmeticEditor scanning the ENTIRE mods archive at startup.

ROOT CAUSE (profiled on-device + sim, 2026-07-24): ScanDynamicCosmetics()
runs once at boot (RefreshDynamicCosmeticsStateIfNeeded, signature-gated) and
does `ListFiles("*")` then, for EVERY file in every custom archive, calls
LoadFile() (zip_fread — decompresses the whole file) just to try parsing it
as a cosmetic-material XML. With a big texture pack that means reading the
WHOLE pack every launch: the user's 4K MM Reloaded pack = ~13 s of pure
zip_fread on the game thread before the first frame (audio underruns to 0).
SoH never pays this (no DynamicCosmeticEditor). Shaders/archive-index are
INNOCENT (they were warm/6 ms while this ran).

FIX: a cosmetic material is a tiny XML DisplayList; textures are megabytes
(this pack: 5011 files >256 KB totalling 2.58 GB, vs 4921 small files at
340 MB). Skip files too large to be a material BEFORE loading them, using a
cheap size query (zip_stat reads the central directory already in memory — no
decompress). Adds Archive::GetFileSize (base default UINT64_MAX = "unknown,
don't skip"), O2rArchive override (zip_stat only), and
ArchiveManager::GetFileSize(path). The scan filter is __IOS__-gated so the
macOS build stays byte-identical; the LUS additions are additive (new
method, no behavior change) so they compile everywhere.

Verify: sim boot with the 4K pack drops from ~13 s to ~2 s (launch->first
Cutscene_HandleConditionalTriggers), and a cosmetic pack's materials still
register (they're < the threshold).

